---
/**
 * Long vs short payoff lines. Uses the same numbers as the prose beside it
 * (short 1 BTC at $70,000, close at $63,000 → +$7,000; the mirror-image long loses $7,000).
 */
---
<figure class="diagram">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 720 320"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="payoff-title payoff-desc"
    preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
  >
    <title id="payoff-title">Profit and loss of a long and a short position as the price moves</title>
    <desc id="payoff-desc">
      Two mirrored straight lines crossing at the $70,000 entry price. The long position gains as the
      price rises and loses as it falls; the short does the opposite. At $63,000 the short is up $7,000
      per BTC and the long is down $7,000 per BTC.
    </desc>

    <!-- axes -->
    <line x1="70" y1="160" x2="690" y2="160" class="axis" />
    <line x1="380" y1="30" x2="380" y2="290" class="axis axis-dim" />

    <!-- payoff lines -->
    <line x1="90" y1="270" x2="670" y2="50" class="line line-long" />
    <line x1="90" y1="50" x2="670" y2="270" class="line line-short" />

    <!-- entry marker -->
    <circle cx="380" cy="160" r="5" class="dot" />
    <text x="380" y="308" class="lbl">Entry $70,000</text>

    <!-- the $63,000 read-off -->
    <line x1="205" y1="94" x2="205" y2="226" class="tie" />
    <circle cx="205" cy="226" r="5" class="dot dot-long" />
    <circle cx="205" cy="94" r="5" class="dot dot-short" />
    <text x="205" y="308" class="lbl">$63,000</text>
    <text x="194" y="116" class="lbl lbl-value lbl-short" text-anchor="end">short +$7,000</text>
    <text x="194" y="210" class="lbl lbl-value lbl-long" text-anchor="end">long −$7,000</text>

    <!-- line labels -->
    <text x="676" y="46" class="lbl lbl-value lbl-long" text-anchor="end">Long</text>
    <text x="676" y="286" class="lbl lbl-value lbl-short" text-anchor="end">Short</text>

    <text x="78" y="154" class="lbl lbl-axis" text-anchor="start">profit</text>
    <text x="78" y="176" class="lbl lbl-axis" text-anchor="start">loss</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Both positions use the same arithmetic — the sign of the price difference flips. A short that
    closes $7,000 below entry earns what the equivalent long would have lost, before fees and
    borrowing costs.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .diagram { margin: 24px 0; }

  .diagram svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 720px;
    display: block;
  }

  .diagram figcaption {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: 10px;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .axis { stroke: var(--color-border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .axis-dim { stroke-dasharray: 4 4; }

  .line { stroke-width: 3; fill: none; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .line-long { stroke: var(--color-primary); }
  .line-short { stroke: #b45309; }

  .tie { stroke: var(--color-border); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 3 4; }

  .dot { fill: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .dot-long { fill: var(--color-primary); }
  .dot-short { fill: #b45309; }

  .lbl {
    fill: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    text-anchor: middle;
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .lbl-value { font-weight: 700; }
  .lbl-long { fill: var(--color-primary); }
  .lbl-short { fill: #b45309; }
  .lbl-axis { font-size: 12px; }

  :global([data-theme='dark']) .line-short,
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .lbl-short,
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .dot-short { stroke: #fbbf24; fill: #fbbf24; }
  :global([data-theme='dark']) .line-short { fill: none; }
</style>
